    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0500" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1072</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-09T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1973. Referring your 2187, January 3, 12 p.m. President delivered speech to
                    Congress yesterday stating war aims and attitude toward Russia. It was cabled
                    you at once.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d422-f1"/> Have it conveyed unofficially to
                    Trotslry. Report results also of measures taken to circulate it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="1" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>The President’s address to Congress of Jan. 8, 1918, containing the “fourteen
                    points” of peace was cabled abroad for publication by the Committee on Public
                    Information.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
